specific" which is similar in meaning to anything.
Anything means something like "of all possible answers to the question of
'what is this about', i choose nothing specific"

"what would you like to eat?" "nothing specific."
.u'i I wouldnt recommend to say that to a waitor though, he might bring you
indeed something unspecific.

"if no-specific pupil would offer himself as the culprit of this prank,
i wouldn't punish the whole class." =
"if any pupil would offer himself as the culprit of this prank, i wouldn't
punish the whole class. "

hm, im not too certain about all this.. what do you think?


